    produced, to within the curve form each writes: Cone matches upstream's
    shield exactly, Polygon its hexagon to 0.002 of 200, Blob to 0.011, Drop
    to 0.046 and Circle to 0.027 (upstream approximates a true arc with
    cubics; the packs write the arc). Two are genuinely different drawings:
    the pack's Capsule has quadratic rather than circular corners (4.55 of
    200) and its Star a different inner radius (12.74 of 200). Each pack's
    face anchor is taken as authored, which is what the rest differ on.
    Not taken: each pack's <Name>Avatar.tsx component, its 65 standalone SVG
    files (svg/states, svg/expressions, svg/sprite.svg), its manifest.json and
    its README.md, and its DEFAULT_GRADIENT (Blob Studio's green — Murage
    paints each body with the bot's own colour). No pack file is vendored into
    this repository. Murage's own src/components/EmberAvatar.tsx already is
    the same generated renderer: each pack's component is byte-identical to it
    apart from the SHAPE constant and that gradient.
    Licence: the packs carry no licence file. Each pack's README states that
    the expression geometry originates in Sebastien Montlouis-Calixte's
    GrokBot prototype gist
